[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: MIL-STD-498 OCD (Operational Concept Document) - Military Quad Copter RTOS
[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 1. Scope
[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 1.1 Identification
[REFERENCE]
TYPE: Document
REF: SRS.sdoc
DESC: See Software Requirements Specification for detailed requirements.
[REFERENCE]
TYPE: Document
REF: SDP.sdoc
DESC: See Software Development Plan for development process.
[[/SECTION]]
[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 1.2 System overview
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: OCD-001-MILUAV
TITLE: System Overview
STATEMENT: The Military Quad Copter RTOS provides autonomous flight, mission management, and secure communication for military UAV operations.
RATIONALE: System overview establishes the context for operational concepts.
[[/SECTION]]
[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 1.3 Document overview
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: OCD-002-MILUAV
TITLE: Document Structure
STATEMENT: This document is organized per MIL-STD-498, covering scope, referenced documents, current system, justification for changes, new system concept, scenarios, and impacts.
RATIONALE: Structured documentation supports review and validation.
[[/SECTION]]
[[/SECTION]]
[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 2. Referenced documents
[REFERENCE]
TYPE: Document
REF: SRS.sdoc
DESC: Software Requirements Specification
[REFERENCE]
TYPE: Document
REF: SDP.sdoc
DESC: Software Development Plan
[[/SECTION]]
[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 3. Current system or situation
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: OCD-003-MILUAV
TITLE: Current Situation
STATEMENT: Current military UAVs use proprietary, non-interoperable flight control software with limited autonomy and security.
RATIONALE: Identifies the need for a new RTOS-based solution.
[[/SECTION]]
[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 4. Justification for and nature of changes
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: OCD-004-MILUAV
TITLE: Justification
STATEMENT: Enhanced autonomy, security, and interoperability are required for next-generation military UAVs.
RATIONALE: Justifies the development of a new RTOS.
[[/SECTION]]
[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 5. Concept for a new or modified system
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: OCD-005-MILUAV
TITLE: New System Concept
STATEMENT: The new RTOS will provide modular, secure, and real-time capabilities for military quad copter operations, supporting advanced autonomy and mission flexibility.
RATIONALE: Describes the operational concept for the new system.
[[/SECTION]]
[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 6. Operational scenarios
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: OCD-006-MILUAV
TITLE: Normal Operations
STATEMENT: The quad copter autonomously executes a reconnaissance mission, reporting real-time video and telemetry to the ground station.
RATIONALE: Demonstrates typical operational use.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: OCD-007-MILUAV
TITLE: Emergency Operations
STATEMENT: On loss of communication, the quad copter returns to base or lands safely using onboard intelligence.
RATIONALE: Demonstrates emergency handling.
[[/SECTION]]
[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 7. Summary of impacts
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: OCD-008-MILUAV
TITLE: Operational Impacts
STATEMENT: The new RTOS will improve mission success rates, reduce operator workload, and enhance security for military UAV operations.
RATIONALE: Summarizes the impact of the new system.
[[/SECTION]]
[[/SECTION]]
